{"id": "cb3833b1-ad56-4df6-8d20-bddabc86f794", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"id": "tooluse_RIE3VybE5dZUBET56UE8IV", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"deep_research": true, "prompt": "{
  "task": "Run the read-only disaster-recovery (DR) readiness data-gathering checks for ONE workload: the CloudFormation stack named 'orders-web' in eu-west-1 (the orders website).",
  "context": "The user wants a DR readiness report for their orders website. Load the 'dr-starting-point' skill yourself (skill_read) and follow its SKILL.md method for Step 0 (map the workload by layer) through Step 5 (check each layer against the four scenarios: single-service failure, AZ failure, Region failure, bad data). You are the subagent in the 'If you delegate data gathering' section of that skill -- DO NOT write the final report or the Step 7 answer. Return ONLY the structured data rows plus the handoff line, exactly as that section specifies: one row per resource in the format 'layer | resource | type | Region | in-Region redundancy (AZs, nodes, tasks) | backups (kind, frequency, retention) | copies, images or IaC outside the Region | point-in-time recovery | replication | what could not be read', followed by the Step 7 outline reminder line.",
  "resources": ["CloudFormation stack: orders-web", "Region: eu-west-1", "AWS account: use the account(s) associated with this agent space -- determine via list_associations/get_association if not obvious; agent space default account is 012345678901_1 but the stack may live in a different associated account -- check and use whichever account actually has a stack named orders-web in eu-west-1"],
  "timeframe": "N/A -- this is a point-in-time configuration/readiness check, not a time-windowed investigation",
  "criteria": "Use cloudformation:ListStackResources on orders-web to enumerate every resource in the stack, then group into layers per the skill's checks-by-layer reference: entry/routing, compute, data, storage, messaging/events, identity, shared dependencies (network, secrets, KMS keys, images, certificates, IaC). For each resource, check: AZ/node/task spread, backup existence and frequency/retention, whether any copy/replica/image/IaC exists outside eu-west-1, point-in-time recovery status, and replication config. Also check AWS Backup plans/vaults covering these resources and whether cross-Region copies actually have landed recovery points (not just configured). Note any resources connected to the stack by configuration (e.g. a database it connects to, secrets it reads, images it pulls) even if not literally inside the stack. Record any denied/skipped API call explicitly as 'not checked' next to that resource. Do not guess a recovery Region -- just report what Regions resources currently exist in."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Gathering DR readiness data for the orders-web CloudFormation stack in eu-west-1."}], "created_at": null}
